the knowledge base module_4_examples includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/module-4-examples.l4".

the person is an adult for an age N if
    N >= 18.

the person is eligible to vote for an age N with a boolean if
    N >= 18
    and true is equal to the boolean.

an age N qualifies for senior discount if
    N >= 65.

the person is a student for an age N with a boolean if
    N >= 16
    and N <= 25
    and true is equal to the boolean.

an income N qualifies for exemption if
    N < 10000.

the tax bracket for an income N is a text if
    N < 10000
    and the text is equal to "exempt"
    otherwise N < 50000
    and the text is equal to "standard"
    otherwise the text is equal to "higher rate".

the income category for an income N is a text if
    N < 20000
    and the text is equal to "low"
    otherwise N < 80000
    and the text is equal to "medium"
    otherwise the text is equal to "high".

the standard deduction is 12000.

the taxable income for a gross income G is a number N if
    the standard deduction is a number M
    and G > M
    and the standard deduction is a number K
    and N = G - K
    otherwise N is equal to 0.

the tax owed for a gross income with a tax rate T is a number N if
    the taxable income for the gross income is a number M
    and N = M * T.

the tax on first bracket for an income is a number N if
    the amount in first bracket for the income is a value V
    and N = V * 0.1.

the tax on second bracket for an income is a number N if
    the amount in second bracket for the income is a number M
    and N = M * 0.2.

the tax on third bracket for an income is a number N if
    the amount in third bracket for the income is a number M
    and N = M * 0.3.

the amount in first bracket for an income N is a value if
    N <= 10000
    and the value is equal to N
    otherwise the value is equal to 10000.

the amount in second bracket for an income N is a number M if
    N <= 10000
    and M is equal to 0
    otherwise N <= 50000
    and M = N - 10000
    otherwise M is equal to 40000.

the amount in third bracket for an income N is a number M if
    N <= 50000
    and M is equal to 0
    otherwise M = N - 50000.

the income tax owed for an income is a number N if
    the tax on first bracket for the income is a number M
    and the tax on second bracket for the income is a number K
    and the tax on third bracket for the income is a number P
    and N = M + K + P.

the standard deduction for a gross income is a number if
    the calculated deduction for the gross income is a number N
    and N >= 1000
    and the calculated deduction for the gross income is the number
    otherwise the number is equal to 1000.

the calculated deduction for a gross income G is a number N if
    N = G * 0.1.

the total deductions for an expenses E with a gross income is a number N if
    the standard deduction for the gross income is a number M
    and N = M + E.

the net income for a gross income G with an expenses is a number N if
    the total deductions for the expenses with G is a number M
    and N = G - M.

an applicant is a qualifying resident if
    the citizenship of the applicant is "citizen".

an applicant is of age if
    the age of the applicant >= 21
    and the age of the applicant < 65.

an applicant meets income threshold if
    the annual income of the applicant < 30000.

an applicant is disqualified if
    the applicant has criminal record.

an applicant is eligible for benefit if
    the applicant is a qualifying resident
    and the applicant is of age
    and the applicant meets income threshold
    and it is not the case that the applicant is disqualified.

the taxpayers bracket for a taxpayer is a text if
    the annual income of the taxpayer is a number N
    and N < 10000
    and the text is equal to "exempt"
    otherwise the annual income of the taxpayer is a number M
    and M < 50000
    and the text is equal to "standard"
    otherwise the annual income of the taxpayer is a number K
    and K < 100000
    and the text is equal to "higher"
    otherwise the text is equal to "top rate".

income requirement is met for an income N with a loan amount L if
    N >= L * 0.3.

credit score is sufficient for a credit score C if
    C >= 650.

debt to income ratio is acceptable for an income N with a loan amount L if
    L <= N * 4.

the loan is approved for an income with a credit score with a loan amount if
    income requirement is met for the income with the loan amount
    and credit score is sufficient for the credit score
    and debt to income ratio is acceptable for the income with the loan amount.

the base premium for a coverage amount C is a number N if
    N = C * 0.001.

the age factor for an insured age N is a number if
    N < 30
    and the number is equal to 1.0
    otherwise N < 50
    and the number is equal to 1.5
    otherwise the number is equal to 2.0.

the smoking factor for a boolean is a number if
    true is equal to the boolean
    and the number is equal to 1.5
    otherwise the number is equal to 1.0.

the annual premium for an insured age with a coverage amount with a boolean is a number N if
    the base premium for the coverage amount is a number M
    and the age factor for the insured age is a number K
    and the smoking factor for the boolean is a number P
    and N = M * K * P.

the late payment penalty for a principal amount P with a days overdue D is a number N if
    D <= 0
    and N is equal to 0
    otherwise D <= 30
    and N = P * 0.02
    otherwise N = P * 0.05.

tenant is in good standing for a late payments with a years as tenant Y if
    Y >= 1
    and 0 is equal to the late payments.

rent is at market rate for a rent R with a market rent M if
    R >= M * 0.9.

a years as tenant qualifies for lease renewal for a late payments with a rent with a market rent if
    tenant is in good standing for the late payments with the years as tenant
    and rent is at market rate for the rent with the market rent.

